---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Notice from "../components/Notice.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const description = `Terms of use for ${site.name}, published by ${site.publisher}.`;
---

<Base title="Terms of Use" description={description}>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="kicker">Terms of Use</p>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.updated}</p>
    <Notice />
    <p>
      These terms are between you and {site.publisher} for {site.name} and for this website. The
      app id is {site.bundleId}. If you do not agree, do not install the game or use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>The game</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a precision game about guiding a living spark of energy home. It is available
      on the <a href={site.appStoreUrl}>App Store</a>. The Android version is
      <a href="/news/play-store-review">in review on Google Play</a>. A feature
      described on this site can change in an update, and a test build may turn some features off.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and play the game
      on devices you own or control, under the rules of the store you use. You do not own the game,
      its art, the name Spark, or its story. You may not copy the game for sale, or modify it,
      except where the law does not allow that limit.
    </p>

    <h2>No account</h2>
    <p>
      The game does not create an account. Progress is stored on your device. We cannot sign you in
      on a new phone, and we cannot recover a save after you delete the app. See
      <a href="/data">Your Data</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Virtual items</h2>
    <p>
      Shards, energy, timed unlimited energy, boosts, and cosmetic sparks and trails exist only
      inside the game. They are a license to use a feature, not a balance of money. They have no
      cash value, and they cannot be transferred or redeemed outside the game. An update may change
      how they work, including cost and availability.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      When the game offers a purchase, Apple or Google charges you and keeps the payment record. We
      do not receive your card number. A refund is requested from Apple or Google under that
      store's rules. Remove Ads stops forced interstitial ads and does not stop optional rewarded
      ads. The details are in the <a href="/advertising">Advertising Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      A store build may show ads as described in the Advertising Policy. That policy is part of
      these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not attack the game or other people through it, do not misuse the support email, and do
      not use the game or this site to break the law.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site describes the game and publishes the privacy, advertising, terms, support, and data
      pages. It does not create an account.
    </p>

    <h2>App stores</h2>
    <p>
      If you download the game from Apple, Apple is not a party to these terms and is not
      responsible for the game or for a claim you have about it. Apple's licensed application terms
      still apply where Apple requires them. If you download it from Google, Google is not
      responsible for the game. The store you used can enforce its own rules, including payment
      rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      The game and this site are provided as they are. We do not promise uninterrupted play, that a
      level will stay unchanged, or that a coming-soon feature will ship on a particular date.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, {site.publisher} is not liable for indirect or consequential
      damages, or for progress that existed only on your device. These terms do not limit a right
      that the law says cannot be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms by posting a new version on this page and changing the date.
      Playing a later version means you accept the terms posted for it. If you do not accept them,
      stop using the game and delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisher}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
